Runes personalize a Practiced working. Practiced mastery opens one socket and
Inscribed mastery opens a second. Use "inscribe <rune> on <working>" to bind a
known pattern and "unbind <rune> from <working>" to lift it without losing
mastery. "Runes <rune>" lists every working that pattern can actually change;
an incompatible rune cannot consume a socket.

Ashkenazy -- Exaltation
  Damaging workings only. Raises their raw power by fifteen percent.

Falx -- Alacrity
  Every working. Shortens its manual cooldown by twenty percent and may also
  quicken a compatible prepared barrage, subject to the ordinary two-round
  floor.

Saloman -- Bastion
  Every SP-costing working. Damaging workings return a small amount based on
  damage, capped at one quarter of discounted ordinary cost. Utility workings
  return ten percent of discounted base cost. Recollection has no SP cost and
  cannot use Saloman. Automatic barrage does not generate a return.

Talek -- Boreal
  Damaging workings only. Adds a separate cold supplement and Chilled.

James -- Whimsy
  Every working. Adds harmlessly unnecessary casting punctuation; Mage Eye and
  Teleport also gain their own ridiculous manifestations.

Marsellus -- Augmentation
  Damaging workings only. Adds a little raw power and a chance for a second
  force impact.

Mezari -- Amity
  Every SP-costing working. Lowers ordinary SP cost by ten percent.
  Recollection has no SP cost and cannot use Mezari.

Ravidel -- Igneous
  Damaging workings only. Adds a separate fire supplement and Burning.

Rodney -- Continuance
  Duration-bearing buffs and controls only: Echoform, Illuminate, Insane,
  Investiture, Invisibility, Levitate, Mana Barrier, Phase, Powerup, Armor,
  Stasis, and Wrath. Extends durations through two minutes by twenty-five
  percent, durations over two minutes by thirty-five percent, and durations
  over five minutes by fifty percent.

Aiken -- Severance
  Damaging workings only. Halves normal armor absorption without bypassing
  resistance, intrinsic reduction, shields, or Mana Barrier.

Arcanarton -- Entropy
  Damaging workings, plus Insane. Adds chaos and disease damage to attacks;
  Insane gains its forbidden variation.

Bodach -- Demise
  Damaging workings, plus Insane and Powerup. Adds death damage and a small
  life return to attacks. It changes Insane's malison and turns Powerup into a
  guarded, pulsing HP-to-SP conversion.

Trivlian -- Putrefaction
  Damaging workings only. Converts their native damage to evil and acid.

Ordinary Arcane study teaches some patterns. Others require mastery, repeated
fire practice, or discoveries on the old Isle of the Magi. Use "runes" for
your current concordance and the exact clue attached to each sealed pattern.
